IMPLICATION FOR THE ALIGNMENT THEOREM:
  the theorem assumes a single symmetric Yukawa.  Every content with
  n_sym = 1 fails (F1 or F2); every viable content has n_sym >= 2 and
  therefore does NOT satisfy the theorem's hypothesis.  The theorem is
  thus a statement that ONE symmetric structure is insufficient, which
  explains why the standard viable model contains two.
